 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Composition: carbon, hydrogen, oxygen and nitrogen (some also sulfur and phosphorus). Proteins are made of units called amino acids.\nSources:\n• animal (high biological value, all the essential amino acids): meat, fish, eggs, milk, snails, crayfish;\n• plant: beans, groundnuts, soya beans, egusi, cowpeas. Mixing plant proteins (beans and maize, as in corn chaff) gives a better mix.\nFunctions: growth, repair of worn tissues, making enzymes, hormones and antibodies; spare protein can give energy.\nDeficiency: kwashiorkor in young children (swollen belly and feet, change of hair colour, poor growth).\nEffects of heat: proteins coagulate (set and harden): egg white becomes white and firm; meat shrinks and hardens if overcooked.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
